boot-repair-legacy (0.2.25-etch1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Legacy Boot Bitch frontend for Debian 4.0 (Etch) / KDE 3.5-era systems:
    the Qt3 GUI (boot-repair-legacy-gui) is the package's entry point. It
    renders the helper's read-only device inventory and Repair tool
    capability lines, greys unavailable tools with their probe reason and
    only enables the legacy-supported commands (including the guarded
    GRUB-legacy regeneration). The shell-only boot-repair-legacy TUI
    launcher, its desktop entry and its man page are no longer shipped.
  * The ported boot-repair-legacy-helper keeps the modern command surface and
    the Repair tool / Repair change status evidence contract on bash 3.1 and
    pre-systemd userlands; the GUI also consumes the probe-based
    Legacy feature lines for the greyed workflows.

 -- CaptainMorgan12 <CaptainMorgan12@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
